Lab 15: Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) in Satellite
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the fundamentals of Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) in Red Hat Satellite
Create and configure custom roles with specific permissions
Assign users to organizations and locations with appropriate access levels
Implement granular permission controls for different user types
Test and validate RBAC policies to ensure proper access restrictions
Troubleshoot common RBAC configuration issues
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux system administration
Familiarity with Red Hat Satellite concepts (organizations, locations, content views)
Knowledge of user and group management in Linux
Understanding of web-based administration interfaces
Completed previous Satellite labs covering basic setup and configuration
